# FS-005 Opportunity Workspace

## 1. Purpose

The Opportunity Workspace provides a unified execution environment for opportunity management within SmartCRM.

The Opportunity Workspace enables users to plan, manage, execute and monitor revenue-generating opportunities throughout their lifecycle.

The Opportunity Workspace serves as the operational center for opportunity execution while reusing information from platform systems of record.

The Opportunity Workspace is designed to support:

- Opportunity Planning
- Opportunity Execution
- Opportunity Collaboration
- Opportunity Intelligence
- Opportunity Governance

The Opportunity Workspace shall provide a single location where users can understand the current state, history, risks, health and progression of an Opportunity.

---

## 2. Scope

### 2.1 In Scope

The Opportunity Workspace includes:

- Opportunity Creation
- Opportunity Ownership
- Opportunity Status Management
- Opportunity Stage Management
- Opportunity Planning
- Opportunity Notes
- Opportunity Timeline
- Opportunity Health
- Opportunity Insights
- SmartAssist Recommendations
- Stakeholder Visibility
- Relationship Intelligence Visibility
- Activity Visibility
- Opportunity Governance

The Opportunity Workspace shall provide a unified execution experience across these capabilities.

---

### 2.2 Out of Scope

The Opportunity Workspace does not own or replace platform systems responsible for:

- Contact Management
- Company Management
- Stakeholder Management
- Relationship Management
- Activity Ownership

Ownership of these capabilities remains governed by their respective SmartCRM specifications.

---

### 2.3 Platform Position

The Opportunity Workspace is not a standalone business capability.

The Opportunity Workspace is a composition layer that brings together reusable SmartCRM capabilities within an Opportunity context.

The Opportunity Workspace shall consume and orchestrate information from platform systems of record.

The Opportunity Workspace shall not duplicate platform ownership responsibilities.

---

## 3. Objectives

### 3.1 Business Objectives

The Opportunity Workspace shall:

- Improve Opportunity Visibility
- Improve Opportunity Execution
- Improve Stakeholder Engagement
- Improve Relationship Coverage
- Improve Forecast Accuracy
- Improve Risk Identification
- Improve User Productivity

The Opportunity Workspace shall support revenue-generating activities throughout the customer lifecycle.

---

### 3.2 User Objectives

Users shall be able to:

- Understand Opportunity Status
- Understand Opportunity Health
- Understand Opportunity Risks
- Understand Stakeholder Coverage
- Understand Relationship Coverage
- View Opportunity History
- Manage Opportunity Execution
- Review SmartAssist Recommendations

Users shall receive actionable information without navigating multiple systems.

---

### 3.3 SmartAssist Objectives

SmartAssist shall:

- Assist Opportunity Owners
- Identify Opportunity Risks
- Identify Coverage Gaps
- Recommend Opportunity Actions
- Highlight Opportunity Trends
- Surface Relevant Context

SmartAssist shall never replace user judgment.

SmartAssist assists.

Users decide.

---

### 3.4 Platform Objectives

The Opportunity Workspace shall:

- Reuse Existing Platform Capabilities
- Preserve System Ownership Boundaries
- Avoid Duplicate Data Stores
- Maintain Single Sources of Truth
- Enable Future Capability Expansion

Future SmartCRM capabilities shall be able to extend the Opportunity Workspace through platform reuse.

---

## 4. Guiding Principles

### 4.1 Opportunity Workspace Principle

The Opportunity Workspace is a reusable execution environment.

The Opportunity Workspace is not a system of record for:

- Contacts
- Companies
- Relationships
- Stakeholders

These records remain owned by their respective SmartCRM specifications.

The Opportunity Workspace consumes platform data and presents it in an Opportunity context.

---

### 4.2 Reality First Principle

The Opportunity Workspace shall comply with the SmartCRM Reality First principle.

The platform shall never present assumptions as verified facts.

Unknown information shall remain unknown until verified.

Reality is preferred over completeness.

Unknown is preferred over fiction.

---

### 4.3 SmartAssist First Principle

SmartAssist shall be available throughout the Opportunity Workspace.

SmartAssist provides insights, recommendations and contextual guidance to support users.

SmartAssist shall remain transparent and explainable.

SmartAssist assists.

Users decide.

---

### 4.4 User Authority Principle

Users remain responsible for:

- Opportunity Decisions
- Opportunity Status Changes
- Opportunity Stage Changes
- Opportunity Closure
- Stakeholder Decisions
- Relationship Decisions

SmartAssist may recommend actions.

Users remain the final decision makers.

---

### 4.5 Single Source of Truth Principle

The Opportunity Workspace shall consume information from platform systems of record.

Ownership remains with the originating specifications.

The Opportunity Workspace shall not create duplicate ownership boundaries.

Platform systems of record remain authoritative.

---

### 4.6 Platform Reuse Principle

The Opportunity Workspace shall reuse platform capabilities wherever possible.

The Opportunity Workspace shall not create duplicate stores for information already managed elsewhere in SmartCRM.

The following principles shall always apply:

- Reuse before duplication
- Composition before replacement
- Integration before replication

Platform reuse is mandatory.

---

### 4.7 Constitution Compliance Principle

The Opportunity Workspace shall comply with:

- SmartCRM Constitution
- SmartAssist Constitution
- Reality First
- SmartAssist First
- User Authority
- Single Source of Truth
- Platform Reuse

Constitutional principles take precedence over implementation decisions.

---

### 4.8 Future Expansion Principle

The Opportunity Workspace serves as the foundational execution environment for future Opportunity-related capabilities.

Future capabilities shall extend the Opportunity Workspace through composition and platform reuse rather than independent ownership models.

The Opportunity Workspace shall remain the primary execution environment for Opportunity management across SmartCRM.

