# 5. Opportunity Ownership

## 5.1 Ownership Principle

Opportunities are first-class business assets.

Every Opportunity shall have an owner.

The Opportunity Owner is responsible for:

- Opportunity accuracy
- Opportunity progression
- Stakeholder engagement
- Opportunity planning
- Opportunity forecasting
- Review of SmartAssist recommendations

---

## 5.2 Ownership Rules

The Opportunity Owner owns the Opportunity record.

The Opportunity Owner does not own:

- Contacts
- Companies
- Relationships
- Activities

Ownership of these records remains governed by their respective SmartCRM specifications.

---

## 5.3 Ownership Independence

Opportunity Ownership exists independently from:

- Contact Ownership
- Company Ownership
- Relationship Ownership

Changes to Contact Ownership shall not automatically modify Opportunity Ownership.

Changes to Company Ownership shall not automatically modify Opportunity Ownership.

Changes to Relationship Ownership shall not automatically modify Opportunity Ownership.

---

## 5.4 Ownership Transfer

Authorized users may reassign Opportunity Ownership.

Ownership transfers shall:

- Be auditable
- Preserve historical ownership information
- Record transfer date and user

Opportunity Ownership changes shall not automatically modify ownership of related records.

---

## 5.5 Opportunity Responsibility

The Opportunity Owner remains accountable for:

- Opportunity progression
- Stakeholder engagement
- Risk mitigation
- Forecast accuracy

SmartAssist may provide recommendations.

The Opportunity Owner remains the final decision maker.

---

# 6. Opportunity Workspace Principles

## 6.1 Workspace Principle

The Opportunity Workspace is a reusable execution environment for opportunity management.

The Opportunity Workspace provides a unified experience for opportunity execution.

The Opportunity Workspace is not a system of record for people, organizations or relationships.

---

## 6.2 Single Source of Truth

The Opportunity Workspace consumes data from platform systems of record.

Ownership remains with the originating specifications.

Examples:

| Data Type | System of Record |
|------------|------------|
| Contacts | FS-002 Contact Management |
| Companies | FS-003 Company Management |
| Relationships | FS-004 Relationship Intelligence |
| Opportunity Stakeholders | FS-001 Opportunity Stakeholder Management |

The Opportunity Workspace shall reuse platform data rather than duplicate it.

---

## 6.3 Platform Reuse Principle

The Opportunity Workspace shall reuse:

- Contact data
- Company data
- Relationship data
- Stakeholder data

The Opportunity Workspace shall not create independent copies of platform data.

Duplicate data stores are prohibited.

---

## 6.4 SmartAssist-First Principle

SmartAssist shall be available throughout the Opportunity Workspace.

SmartAssist may:

- Identify risks
- Recommend actions
- Suggest stakeholder engagement
- Suggest relationship reviews
- Highlight coverage gaps
- Recommend next steps

SmartAssist assists users.

SmartAssist does not make decisions.

---

## 6.5 Reality First Principle

The Opportunity Workspace shall never invent:

- Stakeholders
- Relationships
- Decision Makers
- Influence Chains
- Organization Structures

Unknown information shall remain unknown until verified.

Reality is preferred over completeness.

Unknown is preferred over fiction.

---

## 6.6 User Authority Principle

Users remain responsible for:

- Opportunity decisions
- Opportunity stage changes
- Opportunity closure
- Stakeholder decisions
- Relationship decisions

SmartAssist may recommend.

Users decide.

---

## 6.7 Intelligence Separation Principle

Opportunity Intelligence shall remain separate from Opportunity Facts.

Examples of Opportunity Facts:

- Opportunity Name
- Stage
- Value
- Close Date
- Stakeholders

Examples of Opportunity Intelligence:

- Risk Scores
- Coverage Scores
- SmartAssist Insights
- Recommendations
- Suggested Actions

Intelligence is advisory.

Facts remain system-of-record data.

The Opportunity Workspace shall never store intelligence as verified facts without user confirmation.

---

## 6.8 Composition Principle

The Opportunity Workspace is composed of reusable SmartCRM capabilities.

The Opportunity Workspace shall assemble information from platform systems of record rather than own duplicate copies.

Examples:

- Contacts from FS-002 Contact Management
- Companies from FS-003 Company Management
- Stakeholders from FS-001 Opportunity Stakeholder Management
- Relationships from FS-004 Relationship Intelligence

The Opportunity Workspace serves as an orchestration layer rather than a data ownership layer.

Future capabilities shall be composed into the Opportunity Workspace through reuse of platform services and data sources.

---

## 6.9 Workspace Boundary Principle

The Opportunity Workspace shall orchestrate opportunity execution.

The Opportunity Workspace shall not become a replacement for platform capabilities.

The Opportunity Workspace may surface and consume information from:

- Contact Management
- Company Management
- Opportunity Stakeholder Management
- Relationship Intelligence
- Future Intelligence Capabilities

However, ownership remains with the originating specification.

The Opportunity Workspace shall provide a unified experience while preserving platform boundaries.

Workspace convenience shall never override platform architecture principles.



# 7. Opportunity Model

## 7.1 Opportunity Entity

The Opportunity is the primary business object for revenue-generating pursuits.

```ts
interface Opportunity {
  id: string;

  name: string;

  companyId: string;

  ownerId: string;

  stage: OpportunityStage;

  status: OpportunityStatus;

  value?: number;

  currency?: string;

  probability?: number;

  expectedCloseDate?: string;

  description?: string;

  nextStep?: string;

  createdAt: string;

  updatedAt: string;
}
```

The Opportunity record remains the system of record for opportunity execution.

---

## 7.2 Opportunity Stages

The platform shall support configurable opportunity stages.

Example:

```text
Prospecting
Qualification
Discovery
Proposal
Negotiation
Commitment
Closed Won
Closed Lost
```

Stages may be customized by implementation.

---

## 7.3 Opportunity Status

Opportunity Status represents the lifecycle state of an Opportunity.

The platform shall support the following statuses:

```text
Open
On Hold
Closed Won
Closed Lost
Archived
```

Requirements:

- Status changes shall be auditable.
- Status history shall be retained.
- SmartAssist may recommend status changes.
- SmartAssist shall never perform status changes.
- Users remain responsible for status decisions.
- Archived Opportunities shall remain available for reporting and historical analysis.

---

## 7.4 Opportunity Registry

The Opportunity Registry is the single source of truth for Opportunity records across SmartCRM.

All Opportunity Workspace experiences shall derive Opportunity data from the Opportunity Registry.

Future platform capabilities shall reuse Opportunity data from the Opportunity Registry.

Future capabilities shall not create independent Opportunity stores.

Examples of prohibited patterns:

- Meeting-specific Opportunity stores
- Email-specific Opportunity stores
- Workspace-specific Opportunity stores
- Intelligence-specific Opportunity stores

All Opportunity Intelligence shall derive from the Opportunity Registry.

---

## 7.5 Opportunity Insight

Opportunity Insights are independent advisory records generated by SmartAssist.

Opportunity Insights remain separate from Opportunity Facts.

Example:

```ts
interface OpportunityInsight {
  id: string;

  opportunityId: string;

  type: string;

  observation: string;

  reasoning: string;

  recommendation: string;

  expectedOutcome?: string;

  confidence?: number;

  createdAt: string;
}
```

Opportunity Insights are advisory.

Opportunity Insights are not system-of-record data.

Opportunity Insights shall never automatically modify Opportunity records.

Opportunity Insights shall remain distinguishable from verified Opportunity data.

---

## 7.6 Opportunity Timeline

The Opportunity Workspace shall provide a unified timeline including:

- Meetings
- Calls
- Emails
- Notes
- Stakeholder Changes
- Stage Changes
- SmartAssist Insights

Timeline information shall remain auditable.

---

## 7.7 Opportunity Health

The platform may calculate Opportunity Health.

Inputs may include:

- Stakeholder Coverage
- Relationship Coverage
- Activity Volume
- Opportunity Age
- Stage Progression
- Engagement Trends

Health indicators are advisory.

Users remain responsible for opportunity decisions.

---

## 7.8 Opportunity Fact Principle

Opportunity Facts represent verified business information.

Examples include:

- Opportunity Name
- Company
- Stage
- Status
- Value
- Expected Close Date

Opportunity Facts originate from the Opportunity Registry.

Opportunity Facts shall remain separate from Opportunity Insights.

Opportunity Facts remain authoritative until modified by authorized users.



